            '{"parser": "legacy-migration", "file_name": "jeen buddy guidelines general.docx", "file_type": "docx", "legacyData": {"legacy_id": "4c27d019-6686-43f0-b9a2-102029536cd5", "external_id": null, "collection": "collection", "type": "chunk-data", "tags": "", "user_id": "306916b02924f0142a236cc978b0d013", "create_date": "2026-03-15T07:09:53.896Z", "link_to_file": "https://jeenfilesdevweu.blob.core.windows.net/jeendocs/306916b02924f0142a236cc978b0d013/data/1773558588708-jeen buddy guidelines general.docx", "excerptKeywords": "KEYWORDS: עובד חדש, ארגון, טיפים, תרבות, Jeen.ai"}}'::jsonb,
            '2026-03-15T07:09:53.896000+00:00',
            $TRANS$Make sure the new employee feels comfortable reaching out to you if necessary. To help if necessary in getting to know other people or processes in the organization. Small tips, there is no such thing as a small question, sometimes the most helpful things are actually the informal things, if you don't know something - you can always refer someone else, sometimes a short conversation in the hallway or in Slack makes all the difference ✅, thank you very much for your willingness to take part in the program! This is one of the things that makes our culture in Jeen.ai what it is.$TRANS$
        );
