            '2026-03-15T07:09:53.896000+00:00',
            $TRANS$The first week of the first week is recommended to be a little more present and check in with the new employee on a daily basis how things are progressing. Say hello and introduce yourself on the first day. Schedule a short introductory conversation. Help the new employee understand a little about the team and people. Be available for small questions that arise during the day. Explain how things work on a day-to-day basis in society. Help get to know relevant people in your team or organization. The second week in the second week can be a little less tight, but still stay available and check in from time to time how things are going. Check once every few days how it is going and if there are any questions.$TRANS$
